# **exceptions and rules**

## number of objectives

<p style="font-size: 17px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>NOTE: </strong></span>The <span style="color: darkred;"><strong>plot_hypervolume, plot_GD, plot_GDplus, plot_IGD</strong></span> and <span style="color: darkred;"><strong>plot_IGDplus </strong></span> methods utilize these exceptions and rules.</p>

<p style="font-size: 17px;">All experiments passed as parameters in the method must have the same number of objectives. Otherwise, an exception is thrown.</p>

```python linenums="1"  hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_hypervolume(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, exp4.result)
```

### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>['exp.result = 3 objectives', 'exp2.result = 3 objectives', 'exp3.result = 3 objectives', 'exp4.result = 4 objectives'] must be equals</strong></span></p>


## valid generation interval

<p style="font-size: 17px;">The range of generations must be within the specified range for all experiments.</p>

```python linenums="1" hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_GD(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, exp4.result, generations = [100,450])
```

### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>generations = 450 not be allowed. It must be between 0 and 400</strong></span></p>


## initial and final generation

<p style="font-size: 17px;">The initial generation must be smaller than the final generation.</p>

```python linenums="1" hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_GDplus(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, exp4.result, generations = [600,450])
```

### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>the initial generation must be smaller than the final generation</strong></span></p>


## values ​​for objectives

<p style="font-size: 17px;">No past objective can be greater than the objectives of the experiments.</p>

```python linenums="1" hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_IGD(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, objectives = [1,3,4])
```

### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>Objective(s) ['obj', 'obj', 4] can´t be greather than 3</strong></span></p>


## valid formats

<p style="font-size: 17px;">The parameter format must be followed.</p>

### generations

```python linenums="1" hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_IGDplus(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, exp4.result, generations = 600)
```

#### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>Only arrays are allowed in 'generations'</strong></span></p>



### objectives

```python linenums="1" hl_lines="2"
moeabench.plot_hypervolume(exp.result, exp2.result, exp3.result, exp4.result, objectives = 4)
```

#### exception thrown

<p style="font-size: 15px;"><span style="color: darkred;"><strong>Only arrays are allowed in 'objectives'</strong></span></p>

